  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c0cfaaf7f03baae42a09bb1315032a85, type: 3}
  m_Name: Luzon
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::AreaData
  areaName: Luzon
  dishes:
  - dishName: Longganisang Lucban
    origin: Quezon - CALABARZON (Region IV-A)
    trivia: Lucban's longganisa is garlicky and tangy from vinegar, not sweet like
      many other sausages. Lucban is also home to the colorful Pahiyas Festival every
      May.
    timeLimit: 300
    startingChoices:
    - ingredientName: Ground Pork
      icon: {fileID: 7641075103996889635, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Garlic
      icon: {fileID: 1845359137144016053, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Vinegar
      icon: {fileID: 6433055592894162278, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Sugar
      icon: {fileID: 3956790626070292793, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Salt
      icon: {fileID: 4424271315939866804, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Onion
      icon: {fileID: 8285828631053697030, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    steps:
    - ingredientA: Ground Pork
      ingredientB: Garlic
      resultName: Garlic Pork
      resultSprite: {fileID: -1908011086, guid: c9c56541cd27eec449861f805e40bb4f, type: 3}
      hint: Start with the meat and the garlic.
    - ingredientA: Garlic Pork
      ingredientB: Vinegar
      resultName: Marinated Pork
      resultSprite: {fileID: -893818902, guid: c9c56541cd27eec449861f805e40bb4f, type: 3}
      hint: Marinate the garlicky pork in something sour.
    - ingredientA: Marinated Pork
      ingredientB: Sugar
      resultName: Longganisang Lucban
      resultSprite: {fileID: 4570591547944313421, guid: f7c74d94955595f489083d3202cf56c5, type: 3}
      hint: Lucban longganisa is sweet. Add the final seasoning.
  - dishName: Bulalo
    origin: Batangas - CALABARZON (Region IV-A)
    trivia: Bulalo is named after the bone marrow in the beef shank, the prize of
      the dish. It is a favorite in the cool highlands of Batangas and nearby Tagaytay.
    timeLimit: 300
    startingChoices:
    - ingredientName: Beef Shank
      icon: {fileID: 1049345993608476990, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Marrow Bones
      icon: {fileID: 6463893688377180622, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Water
      icon: {fileID: -2858820527988814422, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Onion
      icon: {fileID: 8285828631053697030, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Corn
      icon: {fileID: -3763835040338069129, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Cabbage
      icon: {fileID: 2829275598139960554, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    steps:
    - ingredientA: Beef Shank
      ingredientB: Marrow Bones
      resultName: Beef Bone Mix
      resultSprite: {fileID: 71129341, guid: c9c56541cd27eec449861f805e40bb4f, type: 3}
      hint: Begin with the two beef parts.
    - ingredientA: Beef Bone Mix
      ingredientB: Water
      resultName: Beef Broth
      resultSprite: {fileID: 914718683, guid: c9c56541cd27eec449861f805e40bb4f, type: 3}
      hint: A soup needs liquid.
    - ingredientA: Beef Broth
      ingredientB: Onion
      resultName: Seasoned Broth
      resultSprite: {fileID: 964456699, guid: c9c56541cd27eec449861f805e40bb4f, type: 3}
      hint: Season the broth with a vegetable.
    - ingredientA: Seasoned Broth
      ingredientB: Corn
      resultName: Corn Beef Soup
      resultSprite: {fileID: 1507598649, guid: c9c56541cd27eec449861f805e40bb4f, type: 3}
      hint: Add the sweet yellow vegetable.
    - ingredientA: Corn Beef Soup
      ingredientB: Cabbage
      resultName: Bulalo
      resultSprite: {fileID: 8209547114987363236, guid: f7c74d94955595f489083d3202cf56c5, type: 3}
      hint: Finish with the leafy green.
  - dishName: Buko Pie
    origin: Laguna - CALABARZON (Region IV-A)
    trivia: Buko means young coconut. This pie is a famous pasalubong from Laguna,
      especially Los Banos, filled with tender coconut strips in a creamy custard.
    timeLimit: 300
    startingChoices:
    - ingredientName: Buko
      icon: {fileID: -976547900972300144, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Sugar
      icon: {fileID: 3956790626070292793, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Milk
      icon: {fileID: 2292363272344975512, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Flour
      icon: {fileID: 134912274554605505, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Butter
      icon: {fileID: -1811272136999082607, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Salt
      icon: {fileID: 4424271315939866804, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    steps:
    - ingredientA: Buko
      ingredientB: Sugar
      resultName: Sweet Buko
      resultSprite: {fileID: -576156222, guid: c9c56541cd27eec449861f805e40bb4f, type: 3}
      hint: Sweeten the coconut.
    - ingredientA: Sweet Buko
      ingredientB: Milk
      resultName: Buko Filling
      resultSprite: {fileID: 425720085, guid: c9c56541cd27eec449861f805e40bb4f, type: 3}
      hint: Make the filling creamy.
    - ingredientA: Flour
      ingredientB: Butter
      resultName: Pie Dough
      resultSprite: {fileID: -506357798, guid: c9c56541cd27eec449861f805e40bb4f, type: 3}
      hint: The crust is made separately from flour and fat.
    - ingredientA: Buko Filling
      ingredientB: Pie Dough
      resultName: Buko Pie
      resultSprite: {fileID: 7582593585184386487, guid: f7c74d94955595f489083d3202cf56c5, type: 3}
      hint: Put the filling and the crust together.
  - dishName: Pastillas
    origin: Bulacan - Central Luzon (Region III)
    trivia: Pastillas de leche is traditionally made from carabao's milk. Bulacan
      sweet makers wrap each candy in paper cut into delicate lace-like patterns
      called pabalat.
    timeLimit: 300
    startingChoices:
    - ingredientName: Milk
      icon: {fileID: 2292363272344975512, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Powdered Milk
      icon: {fileID: -9212022496132874571, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Sugar
      icon: {fileID: 3956790626070292793, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Heat
      icon: {fileID: 988012301, guid: c94253aea3124944fa29318b0a3122a3, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Butter
      icon: {fileID: -1811272136999082607, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Flour
      icon: {fileID: 134912274554605505, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    steps:
    - ingredientA: Milk
      ingredientB: Powdered Milk
      resultName: Milk Mixture
      resultSprite: {fileID: 1452212299, guid: c9c56541cd27eec449861f805e40bb4f, type: 3}
      hint: Two kinds of milk go first.
    - ingredientA: Milk Mixture
      ingredientB: Sugar
      resultName: Sweet Milk
      resultSprite: {fileID: -986690363, guid: c9c56541cd27eec449861f805e40bb4f, type: 3}
      hint: Make it sweet.
    - ingredientA: Sweet Milk
      ingredientB: Heat
      resultName: Pastillas
      resultSprite: {fileID: -652053440740120767, guid: f7c74d94955595f489083d3202cf56c5, type: 3}
      hint: Cook it down until it can be rolled.
  - dishName: Sinaing na Tulingan
    origin: Batangas - CALABARZON (Region IV-A)
    trivia: Sinaing means slowly cooked. Tulingan is simmered for hours in a clay
      pot with kamias and salt until even the fish bones turn soft enough to eat.
    timeLimit: 300
    startingChoices:
    - ingredientName: Tulingan
      icon: {fileID: -6024271103639268514, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Salt
      icon: {fileID: 4424271315939866804, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Kamias
      icon: {fileID: 2385208702603898473, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Water
      icon: {fileID: -2858820527988814422, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Vinegar
      icon: {fileID: 6433055592894162278, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    - ingredientName: Garlic
      icon: {fileID: 1845359137144016053, guid: dadea98780536f0489ec0b51eee7d2d9, type: 3}
    steps:
    - ingredientA: Tulingan
      ingredientB: Salt
      resultName: Salted Tulingan
      resultSprite: {fileID: 959235504, guid: c9c56541cd27eec449861f805e40bb4f, type: 3}
      hint: Season the fish first.
    - ingredientA: Salted Tulingan
      ingredientB: Kamias
      resultName: Sour Tulingan
      resultSprite: {fileID: -593308976, guid: c9c56541cd27eec449861f805e40bb4f, type: 3}
      hint: The sour fruit softens the fish.
    - ingredientA: Sour Tulingan
      ingredientB: Water
      resultName: Sinaing na Tulingan
      resultSprite: {fileID: 6047284333949239989, guid: f7c74d94955595f489083d3202cf56c5, type: 3}
      hint: Slow-cook it with water.
